MID_SE_Led_Max_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_001: Hey, Jester! Have a minute?
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_002: What? I'm getting bored already just looking at\nyour face.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_003: Now, we could put a little red on it, spruce it up.\nThat'd keep me entertained! Heh heh HEH!
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_004: Oh, sure. I've had my face painted red many times,\nwith the blood of my enemies.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_005: Urkh... Hah hah... Now that's fun!
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_006: Do you think so? You know, I think you and I could\nget along famously.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_007: Uh-huh. So you dress like a bard, but you're covered\nin blood stains. You really an assassin or something?
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_008: In a sense. But really I'd prefer not to be lumped in\nwith that unsavory crowd.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_009: My target is in Dagsion. A man they call the\nWhite-Maned Demon—whose real name is Bertrand.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_010: Huh?! Right... Killing the man who beat a giant.\nSmall potatoes. Guess you want my help, huh?
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_011: Exactly. You do seem to be in contact with him.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_012: Hyehe. Sure, I'll help! How much coin you going\nto put in my purse?
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_013: Oh, it's money you want. That's a surprise. I didn't\ntake you for the profit-motivated type.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_014: Well, it's no matter. After I achieve my goal I can pay\nyou whatever amount you ask for.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_015: I got some fixations of my own—but yours is\ndifferent. Why do you want him dead so bad?
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_016: Heh. Do the specifics matter? The White-Maned\nDemon's given plenty of people reason to hate him.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_017: The heartless brute's been kept in that arena for\nso long now.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_018: That's...stupid. I don't kill people for stupid reasons.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_019: Kill him? Oh, you misunderstood me.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_020: Er. What?
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_021: I'm going to kill him. All I need from you is\ninformation.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_022: *gasp* Alright... Tell ya what. We'll talk about it\nsomewhere more quiet.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_023: He gets reaaal angry when he's frustrated. Oh,\nand he favors his left leg—injured it a ways back.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_024: Your honesty's appreciated. Here—by way of thanks.\nI hope we'll continue working together.
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_025: Whew. We're the same age. But she's got that cold\nlook in her eyes...
MID_SE_Led_Max_C_026: The look of someone who wants to kill. If she figures\nout I'm lying, then...
MID_SE_Led_Max_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_001: U-uh, Leda!
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_002: Maxim. Hm.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_003: Seeing your face always reminds me how clouded my\neyes were.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_004: I mean, I tried to get reliable information from the\nman who was Bertrand's squire in Cydonia!
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_005: Of course everything you told me was useless. Or just\nplain wrong.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_006: You were in good company. I should've recognized\nyou too, after the order Bertrand gave me that day.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_007: He told me to persuade you to come back. But I\nthought you were dead until I saw you in the arena.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_008: Hm. It wouldn't have mattered if you recognized\nme. I was not to be persuaded.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_009: No, I guess not. You still want him dead.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_010: *sigh*
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_011: I can tell. I spent some time with a group called the\nOrder of the Haze.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_012: I got good at seeing when people have murder in\ntheir hearts. And you still do.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_013: Yes, I do. So what? I guess you'd better kill me, huh?
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_014: No. Why would I do that?
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_015: What kind of question is that? I'm the enemy of the\nperson you serve.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_016: Sure...but you're trying to protect him too.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_017: That's probably not what you want to hear.\nBut there's a reason you're helping us in our fight.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_018: Th-that's not— I just don't want him to\nget killed by someone else!
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_019: Leda, I don't know all that's in your heart.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_020: But I think you're a kinder person than you\nwant to admit.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_021: You're...impossible. Fine! Believe what you want.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_022: How annoying that I've lost again.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_023: Huh? Lost how?
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_024: I've done more than my fair share of lying. Tricked\nall manner of people.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_025: But I couldn't see Jester's true identity through the\nlayer of deception. He's a consummate con artist.
MID_SE_Led_Max_B_026: Nah, not an artist. He's just...a clown. Heh HEH.